h1. Testing Summary

*Test Coverage: 45 test cases total*
* Automated: 32 cases (71%)
* Partially Automated: 8 cases (18%)
* Manual Only: 5 cases (11%)

*Test Categories:*
* Positive scenarios (7): Upload, display, carousel, edit, delete operations
* Negative scenarios (6): Invalid formats, oversized files, missing fields, unauthorized access
* Boundary tests (6): File size limits, max banners, character limits
* Security tests (6): XSS, SQL injection, malicious files, concurrent edits
* Non-functional tests (8): Performance, lazy loading, CDN, responsiveness, accessibility
* Integration tests (3): CMS to homepage data flow, cache invalidation
* Regression tests (2): Existing features, homepage layout

*Automation Tools:* Playwright for E2E testing, RSpec for backend tests

h1. Technical Implementation Summary

h2. Architecture
* *Service Objects*: BannerUploadService, BannerImageProcessorService
* *Query Objects*: ActiveBannersQuery, ScheduledBannersQuery
* *Presenters*: BannerPresenter for API responses
* *Background Jobs*: BannerActivationJob, BannerExpirationJob
* *Authorization*: Pundit policies for admin-only access

h2. Database Schema
* New {{banners}} table with fields: title, alt_text, click_through_url, priority, status, placement, start_date, end_date, display_order, metadata (JSONB)
* Active Storage for image management with responsive variants (desktop, tablet, mobile, thumbnail)
* Indexes on: status, placement, composite indexes for query optimization
* Zero-downtime migrations with {{strong_migrations}} gem

h2. Key Features
* Image validation (type, size, dimensions)
* Responsive image variants via Active Storage
* Caching strategy (5-minute cache, CDN integration)
* Scheduled activation/expiration via background jobs
* XSS and SQL injection protection
* Comprehensive error handling and logging

h2. Performance Optimizations
* Fragment caching for API responses
* Eager loading to prevent N+1 queries
* CDN integration for image serving
* Partial indexes for active banners
* Image optimization and lazy loading

h2. Security Measures
* Pundit authorization (admin-only)
* Input sanitization (XSS protection)
* File type validation (prevent malicious uploads)
* CSRF protection
* SQL injection prevention via parameterized queries

h1. Implementation Phases (5 weeks)

*Week 1:* Database, models, validations, service objects
*Week 2:* Controllers, API endpoints, background jobs, authorization
*Week 3:* Admin UI, frontend integration, carousel component
*Week 4:* Testing (unit, integration, security, performance), documentation
*Week 5:* Deployment to staging, gradual production rollout, monitoring

h1. Dependencies & Risks

*Dependencies:*
* CMS admin access (https://ide.ioh.co.id/cms/login)
* Active Storage configured
* CDN setup (recommended)
* Platinum Business Hub Homepage deployed

*Risks & Mitigations:*
* Large files impact performance → Strict 2MB limit + optimization
* Browser compatibility → Well-tested carousel library + cross-browser testing
* Concurrent edits → Last-save-wins with timestamps

